th no  real lore behind them i get it there's a  lot of them but like i said i would have  preferred them to half the amount of  optional bosses and really build up  those bosses than just throw random  re-skinned trolls five or six times but  that's just me now let's talk about the  bread and butter when it comes to from  software games the gameplay i've always  felt like they perfected this type of  gameplay where people have adapted it to  a point and you've seen it sprinkle a  little bit throughout the industry in  terms of other games and eldon ring  doesn't seem to be any exception it  seems that they took that existing  formula and they made it better now is  anything different no i've always been  one of those people that says you don't  have to do stuff different just do it  better than you did it previously got a  lot of fans that have been buying from  software games for the past 10 years  that love that type of gameplay from  from software so i don't expect them to  really change it too too drastically now  what i've always enjoyed about from  software games and they really deliver  on here is the diversity gameplay they  let you play these how you want to play  you can play as a mage you can play as a  faith user you could play as a warrior  and you could play something that's a  little bit of overall thing where they  have multiple of those things in one  build where you know you have a warrior  with some faith enhancements or you know  you're worried that you throw some  spells in there there and the best part  about everything i said is that is  entirely up to you how you want to play  eldon ring weapons is returning  obviously in eldon ringing i could say  they're actually pretty well done the  majority of these weapons feel unique  they they feel nice when you attack them  and what i've really always enjoyed  about from software games and eldon ring  is no exception is when you see someone  use something generally you can snatch  that thing when you see someone have  armor on that you like oh that looks  pretty nice you can generally farm them  for that or sometimes if you can't farm  them you can find those weapons or find  that armor somewhere around the map now  obviously from software changed the  formula that they normally do most of  their games are kind of linear with a  little bit of branching opportunities in  terms of map design now from software  has always been masters of how they do  the map design but they've never went  full blown open world and they did that  with eldon ring and i can honestly say  that from software is one of the few  companies with developers that i've seen  attempt to do a full open world and do  it flawlessly is there issues with the  open world of course there's nothing  perfect in gaming nothing is i do feel  like some things could have been  differently in terms of you know how the  world unfolds now what's really cool on  here is there is actually like a day and  night cycle so there'll be more heavy  bosses come out at night there'll be  bosses in general just chilling  everywhere you can go around a random  field and band there's a dragon you can  go under some you know volcano band  there's like some fire wavering like i  really enjoy the sensation of just  traveling in eldon ring now clearly a  lot of you that's watching this you see  how hyped how successful eldon ring is  and i think this key point is why it's  successful when you have a player that's  never really played from software games  or maybe they hate from software games  you know kind of the person i used to be  in terms of from software back in the  old days with the demon souls the dark  souls uh you know sacro some of them had  a little bit of options that you could  do besides the boss that you were stuck  on but for the most part you were stuck  there till you beat that boss elder ring  it's not really the case now if you get  beat too many times fighting the boss in  eldon ring you can simply leave you're  not made to go there now sure some of  these times you'll get stuck on a main  boss and there's a couple of them in the  game but for the most part the amount of  bosses that's in this game overweigh the  amount of main bosses for example main  bosses is people you have to defeat to  continue the storyline you don't have to  do any of them for a long time for the  most part you can go on and do what you  want to do you could travel to my parts  of the map that you really shouldn't be  at you go to a part of the map that  you're not supposed to be there and  guess what you get one-shotted but the  ability is they give you the option if  you want to continue down that route or  do you want to turn around and level up  a little bit now obviously when it comes  to this this is what sold them i'm  confident that this game is going to  sell a lot of units just based off of  this and this alone it's inviting people  to play this game that doesn't really  have the experience of from software  games while keeping their hardcore  audience happy i'm really enjoying the  fact that they did this and didn't  really try to casualize the game too too  much now there's obviously issues with  elden ring in terms of you know i felt  like some of the lore could have totally  been better but i don't think none of  this really takes away from the fact of  how special this game is and i feel like  this is the kind of game that we only  get once every few years to maybe once a  generation from software has done such a  fantastic job explaining to people what  they need to do and explaining to people  why they need to buy this game giving  people the freedom the diversity to play  the game how they want that they did a  lot of things that i wouldn't  necessarily think would be possible in  modern time they've already sold 12  million copies keep in mind that the  iron lords podcast has bought three  copies of these because we wanted to  stream it we wanted to give the opinions  of myself on the review we bought three  copies so i know this game's doing good  eldon ring deserves your money there i'm  just going to say they deserve your  sixty dollars i do feel like there's a  lot of things that is wrong with elder  marine but the positive  drastically outweighs the negatives and  i think they deserve your money on  multiple times if you want a double dip  this is the only time i'll probably ever  say it's okay to double dip i'm not  really the biggest fan of double dipping  but if you want to play this on another  platform to play with your other friends  because it's not cross play or cross  progression i don't blame you that's how  good this game is eldon ring is the type  of game that i will be playing or  thinking about for years to come and i'm  kind of sad that my journey with this  game pretty much is over now i will be  playing the new game plus because it has  a new game plus but i don't know how  much long i'll play after that new game  plus has started because i'm the kind of  person that once a game has concluded  and i can't really get any more  information story wise normally i will  slowly drop the game after that now this  game might be different because i do  want to go back and i want to try some  of these overpowered mage builds i hear  about i want to try more of these  weapons that i've gotten that i don't  really need right now because i got kind  of a lock on the type of weapons that i  want to use i want to try all this stuff  and it has a lot of replayability but i  don't know if i'll actually go back and  replay these games it's like i said i  put 100 plus hours in this game and i'm  still constantly playing it and that  pretty much concludes the review of  eldon rank for the xbox series x it's  like i said solid graphics nothing  special nothing's gonna blow your mind  it's not like the state of the art in  terms of eye candy for the xbox or  anything in that matter because i've  seen it on the playstation five and i've  seen it on pc i'm sure the pc version  looks a lot better but as far as like  what the core graphics look like it's  nothing special performance is iffy  sometimes not a whole lot now it's like  i said i did not play this game before  the game came out when i was having the  most issues but i had a relatively solid  experience and the game plays probably  second to none it's an amazing gameplay  of diversity in games where you know if  you want to play as a mage cool you want  to play as a warrior cool if you want to  place everything wonderful they give you  the option they give you the freedom to  do so and that's the review for eldon  ring so definitely hit that like button  if you guys enjoyed this review it's  like i said man iron lords podcast we do  a podcast every 1pm on sunday definitely  tune into that you know we talk about  games such as eldon ring and pretty much  everything in the industry and until  next lord's review this is lord addict  i'm out of here peace
 

